        "solution": "\u003cp>The model and Swift Testing blocks above are the worked answer. In your scratch package, run \u003ccode>swift test\u003c/code> beside Package.swift. The four named Swift Testing tests should pass for the shown implementation. Adding the optional XCTest example adds another test. A successful compile is separate from a completed test run; record which one you actually performed.\u003c/p>\u003cp>With the deliberately incorrect try? fallback, offline becomes loaded with an empty array. The expected offline state and inequality assertions fail, exposing the lost retry information. Restoring the explicit catch repairs the behavior. That exercise demonstrates why the test matters independently of the particular implementation.\u003c/p>\u003cp>A useful remaining requirement is whitespace-only query normalization: our rule checks empty strings, not trimmed content. Another is localization of the display messages. A stored callback would need an escaping parameter and an ownership graph; this package currently stores no callbacks. Present these as limits, not as bugs secretly fixed by a passing test run. The course author's verification of snippets is separate from your own lab completion.\u003c/p>"
