        "solution": "\u003cp>The detail needs local message storage. Put that storage in a small stateful child rather than adding independent state to the destination closure. Use the child below inside the detail's VStack. Its binding changes the text passed to the existing UIKit controller.\u003c/p>\u003cpre>\u003ccode class=\"language-swift\">struct DetailMessage: View {\n    let id: String\n    @State private var suffix = \"\"\n\n    var body: some View {\n        VStack {\n            UIKitMessage(message: id + suffix)\n            Button(\"Update message\") { suffix = \" — updated\" }\n        }\n    }\n}\u003c/code>\u003c/pre>\u003cp>Use \u003ccode>DetailMessage(id: id)\u003c/code> from the route destination. The update calls \u003ccode>display\u003c/code> on the existing represented controller. The audited outcome table should say selection → selected value; explicit cancel/back/modal swipe → cancelled; invalid initial input → reported bug then cancelled after alert dismissal; search-no-results → stay active. In the current code, optional common-procedure work is cancelled by explicit result paths and interactive modal dismissal. The pushed removal callback finishes cancellation; the base finish stores and delivers its result without cancelling subclass task handles. This source-observed cleanup difference is a review question, not a demonstrated runtime defect. The address host must receive full child containment so UIKit can route controller events.\u003c/p>"
