      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Write an RFC and scratch prototype for first-occurrence slot mapping. Deliver the decision, exact expected fixtures, evidence plan, and recovery limits. Leave client sources untouched.",
        "steps": [
          "State the problem, affected callers, scope exclusions, and exact first-value and ordering rules.",
          "Describe the old adapter and candidate behind SlotMapping.",
          "Write full expected slot values, including duplicate IDs with conflicting titles and selection after replacement.",
          "Compare at least three options. Name a measurement or failure that would reject your preferred option.",
          "Follow source and test inclusion through the module and booking manifests.",
          "Define rollout, containment, and removal conditions. Mark every evidence entry as planned or actually executed."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "The RFC asks for a bounded decision with named owners",
          "Ordering and duplicate-value semantics are explicit",
          "Performance and behavioral evidence are separate",
          "Accessibility, privacy, and build-path concerns appear in the plan",
          "Recovery applies only to honoring clients and does not promise a store downgrade",
          "No actual deployment or client migration is claimed"
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>The worked RFC is titled “Keep first-occurrence slot mapping behind a tested value contract.” It asks about a synthetic large-list membership cost. The scope excludes UI replacement, storage-format changes, and network submissions. Its contract preserves input order, case-sensitive IDs, and each first complete slot without mutating the input. These exact promises make the proposal reviewable before any timing or rollout claim.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The equivalence fixture contains \u003ccode>a/First\u003c/code>, \u003ccode>b/Second\u003c/code>, and \u003ccode>a/Replacement\u003c/code>; expected output is the first two complete values. Comparing IDs alone would miss an accidental last-title policy. Empty, all-duplicate, and all-distinct inputs complete the minimal matrix. A separate consumer test changes the array order while preserving a selected ID, then verifies the selection still points to that ID.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Option B is provisionally selected over unchanged scans and new async scheduling. The measurement plan compares several input sizes, records release/device conditions and memory cost, and then measures action-to-usable-results. Until those observations exist, the benefit is a hypothesis. The proposed dependency seam follows the concept of the actual module protocol, while the pure mapper remains free of UI actor annotations.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Milestones are characterize, adapt, implement, compare, measure, integrate, observe, and remove. Characterization requires expected full-value results; integration requires source/test inclusion in both relevant graphs during coexistence. Rollout records mapping-version cohorts using approved bounded telemetry. Containment uses the old pure implementation only if the installed binary contains an honored selection path. Removal requires stable outcomes and owner agreement that the duplicate path is no longer needed.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The decision request is approval for this bounded experiment, not approval for a completed migration. The evidence ledger marks device accessibility, end-to-end timing, archive verification, and production impact as planned. A reviewable proposal with those limits is useful even before implementation; it must not be presented as observed team or customer impact.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Use ExistingSlotAdapter, scanningSlots, and verifySlotPrototype from the adapter section as the worked prototype, with the shared SyntheticSlot and FirstOccurrenceMapper declarations. Run the five expected-value fixtures before timing either implementation. Record the actual invocation and outcome; source text alone leaves equivalence execution pending. A successful migration retires the old scan and temporary adapter after adoption and recovery review. Rejecting the experiment retires the candidate instead. Name the mapper owner for that debt and keep only the selected permanent contract.\u003c/p>"
      },
