      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Build DemoCodeForm in a scratch target. Check raw text, UTF-16 replacement, and keyboard behavior, then record what you observed.",
        "steps": [
          "Try an empty or whitespace-only name, code 01234, pasted letters, non-ASCII digits, and replacement of selected text.",
          "Use replacingDemoText to replace the emoji in A🙂B with X at NSRange(location: 1, length: 2). Explain why those are UTF-16 units.",
          "Add persistent field labels and localized field errors while keeping one owner for each raw buffer.",
          "Try Done on the number pad, submit with a hardware keyboard, and error recovery at narrow width with larger text.",
          "Use a keyboard that composes characters. Record marked-text and cursor behavior, then compare it with the active model's normalization code."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "01234 remains a string with its leading zero.",
          "The synthetic rule accepts exactly five ASCII digits and rejects other characters at submission.",
          "Replacing the emoji yields AXB without corrupting surrounding text.",
          "Done dismisses input without clearing the buffers, and invalid submission focuses a repairable field.",
          "The record distinguishes model-rule checks from actual keyboard and composition observations."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>The demo form accepts name Demo Ada and code 01234, keeps the code as typed, and shows its synthetic success status. Five Arabic-Indic digits fail this particular ASCII-only rule; that is not a judgment about valid codes in other systems. The repository's isWholeNumber rule is broader and must be described separately. A name made only of spaces stays editable but cannot be submitted. On an invalid attempt, keep both text buffers and request the first field needing repair. The example sends no request.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For A🙂B, the UTF-16 representation has four code units: A, the emoji's surrogate pair, and B. Replacing location 1, length 2 with X yields AXB. Deleting a selected range uses the same helper with an empty replacement. A conversion failure returns nil; the caller must choose a safe no-edit or diagnostic policy rather than force-unwrapping it.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Provide localized labels and an error that names which rule failed. Keep the explicit Done path because submitLabel cannot supply a missing number-pad Return key. Test composition and selection through the real input method; a pure string helper cannot certify that experience. The report should identify the keyboard, OS, width, text category, and observed outcome, while marking unexecuted device fixtures pending. No live data or client submission is part of this exercise.\u003c/p>"
      },
