        "story": "Kabir has ten trays to wash and three sinks. He starts trays 0, 1, and 2. Tray 2 finishes first, so he puts its result in the slot labeled 2 and starts tray 3 in the freed sink. He does not hire ten workers to stand around holding wet trays while waiting. When someone asks him to stop, he stops admitting new trays and asks active workers to finish or stop safely. A waiting list, the number of occupied sinks, and the order of finished results are different limits.",
