        "solution": "\u003cp>The retained package declares ZDModulesMocks as dynamic. Its sibling Project.swift declares a staticFramework. Record both facts and identify their test consumers before proposing a change. Similar names do not establish identical packaging. For lottie-spm, write down branch 4.1.3 and the commit in the relevant resolution file. The branch’s numeric name does not turn it into an exact-version requirement. This is a source comparison, not an observed runtime defect or a completed linkage test.\u003c/p>\u003cp>VendorCodec's contract names its consumer product, supported device and simulator variants, minimum OS, public interfaces, linked dependencies, resource bundles, privacy information, checksum, and origin evidence. License and vulnerability decisions remain pending until the selected artifact and its dependencies are reviewed. Module-version failure suggests interface/toolchain inspection; duplicate symbols suggest repeated definitions or linkage; a loader failure suggests embedding and run paths; a nil resource URL suggests bundle membership and lookup.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Reconstruction uses the prior manifest, relevant resolution file, source revision or binary checksum, generator and compiler versions, and unchanged resource inputs. A narrow source-package build can establish a compilation boundary, while an app or test-host build checks integration. Packaging and device execution require their own evidence. This is a worked review, not proof that either observed linkage route or the synthetic binary has been executed.\u003c/p>"
