        "story": "Tara prepares a visitor badge for Alex. The badge is ready only after the front desk finishes checking it. Before that happens, Alex’s visit is canceled and Bea arrives. A late call says Alex’s badge is ready. Tara does not open the door for Alex or attach that badge to Bea’s visit. She checks the current visit number first. Even a current badge lets a visitor use only the agreed rooms, not ask the building staff to carry out any command.",
        "meaning": "Cookie setup and authentication finish asynchronously. An account or attempt can change while they wait. A web bridge must offer only small allowed operations, and callbacks must still belong to the current account and document.",
