        "solution": "\u003cp>The full core, manifest, and test block above form the package answer. The core plus smoke block form the standalone answer. Choose the route matching your scratch layout and record the toolchain, command, exit result, and final summary. The package defines five Swift Testing tests. Its runner may also report zero XCTest tests in a compatibility preamble; read the final Swift Testing summary before deciding whether the five functions ran.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The deliberate errors-to-empty mutation should fail malformed, nonpositive and unexpected-failure expectations while successful empty input still passes. That shows the tests defend domain distinctions instead of mirroring implementation structure. Restore explicit classification before keeping your completed scratch answer. The lifetime test establishes a weak owning edge and safe missing-owner path; it proves no producer cancellation because the program has no producer work.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For a changed exercise, parse [4, 6] and predict loaded([4, 6]), then parse [-1] and predict failed(nonpositive(-1)). Explain how an accept-valid-rows policy would require an output carrying rejection evidence rather than merely changing compactMap. Optional matching guides can deepen construction, generic contracts and callback ownership afterward. Author verification does not pre-complete the learner’s attempt; readiness depends on independent implementation, explained predictions and a documented remaining-practice plan.\u003c/p>"
