        "solution": "\u003cp>The named previews supply the required cases. The empty fixture displays No display name. The long-name fixture increases text size while keeping its stored String unchanged. In the editable host, the card reads the same name the field edits. A constant-binding field is useful only as a frozen sample; it does not own changing storage. Compare those cases so you can explain the difference between showing an input and allowing the user to change it.\u003c/p>\u003cp>A worked evidence note lists the canvas scenarios actually rendered, then a separate simulator Run of FixtureHost. If the preview fails to build, record the first diagnostic and verify the view in the app before blaming state. For a future dependency fixture, construct the model in the host and pass it explicitly or install it through environment at that boundary. Do not add a production fallback to make the canvas appear. The older provider is an alternative declaration form, and official release notes determine backward-deployment details; no deployment change or real network access is required by this lesson's baseline.\u003c/p>"
