        "solution": "\u003cp>ObservedRoot stores the ReadingDraft reference in State. ObservedEditor uses Bindable to give TextField and Toggle access to its fields. DraftSummary only reads the same instance. Empty or spaces-only names show Enter a name; Demo Ada shows that current name. Reset changes fields on the same object. Model checks in a unit-test target must follow its MainActor access rules too.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The legacy owner instead uses StateObject with a LegacyDraft conforming to ObservableObject, and its consumer uses ObservedObject. Both alternatives are internally consistent; mixing only their wrappers is not. A correct source audit identifies the address demo's creator and retained coordinator, then marks the member-ID consumer's upstream ownership as something to trace rather than guessing it. If you add persistence later, record its save/load and account-boundary rules separately. These steps provide a worked answer and expected behavior, not a claim that either target was launched or migrated here.\u003c/p>"
