        "solution": "\u003cp>Start with the eligibility and Reset model checks. In the gated test, A2 publishes Current A2. Later A1 success is ignored, and the old B error cannot replace that value or set the error. The token names the request generation independently of the text. ControlledSuggestion intentionally ignores cancellation while waiting so those late paths really run. Extend the design with an invalidation-only check and an old A1 error. A complete test harness must finish all waiting requests even if setup fails.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The UI sequence should end with an empty name and disabled Review under the supplied English fixture, but query details must match the actual runtime hierarchy. Cancel with an existing topic must preserve it because no cancel action assigns topic. A final note should list actual test command/action, destination, outcome and unresolved failures. If only source type checking was possible, state that; linking, Run and interaction remain pending. No persisted draft, company source change or real request is part of this capstone. Compare with the SwiftUIWorkbench companion using its actual source and recorded verification; a build result does not establish app interaction.\u003c/p>"
