        "story": "Leena has a paper draft. She can give a sealed copy of its text to a colleague and keep editing her own paper. Or she can hand over the original and stop using it. If she keeps a second key to the drawer holding that original, the handoff is incomplete: two people could still edit the same sheet. After a complete handoff, the colleague keeps the paper in a controlled workspace and sends Leena a read-only report. Handing over that one sheet does not make every sheet in the workshop safe for everyone to edit.",
