        "meaning": "Allocation reserves storage; initialization starts the values' lifetimes. Reads must stay within initialized storage. Deinitialization ends those lifetimes, then deallocation releases the allocation. A returned Int can outlive the storage. Borrowed pointers have a limited validity window, not independent ownership.",
