        "acceptance": [
          "The same child identity moves rows when its key changes.",
          "A narrower width recalculates row membership and height.",
          "Every first baseline within a row agrees under the declared metric policy.",
          "Logical coordinates preserve child order and nonzero bounds offsets; native RTL reflection is verified separately.",
          "Editing progression and assistive error focus are recorded independently on an identified destination."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>Keep the same child and change only its row-break value. Add @State private var forceBreak = false and a semantic Toggle in the fixture view. Apply .layoutValue(key: RowBreakKey.self, value: forceBreak) to the child's stable declaration. The cache signature already includes breakBefore, so this change requires a new arrangement even if sizes and child count stay the same. A zero-height Spacer would instead change the child set and make the row-break contract harder to see.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the existing shared metrics, the forty-by-twenty and fifty-by-thirty children fit in width one hundred twenty with an eight-point gap. Their baseline-aligned row height is thirty. At width seventy they occupy separate rows, so the total height becomes twenty plus twelve plus thirty, or sixty-two. The host checks assert those values. The wide logical x origins remain zero and forty-eight; their y offsets are five and zero. SwiftUI performs the RTL reflection at placement, which these host tests do not exercise. The host suite also toggles the second child's break flag at the same wide width and verifies a new row without changing dimensions.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Use actual Text dimensions for the next stage. Increase Dynamic Type and change the label to a long localized string; the remeasured fingerprint should change as needed. Record clipping, line breaks, and scroll reachability. If a child returns a width wider than its proposal, the helper preserves its logical origin and allows width overflow; a product may instead require an adaptive stacked alternative. Do not claim the helper repaired an uncooperative child's measurement.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For interaction, verify both axis-specific scrolls and diagonal gestures, then edit Name, submit to Note, use Previous/Next/Done, and submit an empty name. Record software keyboard visibility and hardware traversal separately from VoiceOver's announcement of the error. The app already supplies these affordances, but their runtime results remain pending here. Container-level explicit baseline guides, same-axis nested fling transfer, complex rich-text layout, and assistive-technology user testing are separate specialist extensions. The worked answer defines expected contracts without completing the learner's acceptance notebook.\u003c/p>"
