        "solution": "\u003cp>Fix a repeatable setup before starting the timer. Choose the shared ProfilingLab scheme and Release Profile action. Keep image, caption and worker choices fixed. Prepare the synthetic PNG before recording and name worker-entry-to-model-ready as the main metric. The expected ordered result is Row 0 café through Row 1499 café. The host check compares both complete arrays, handles empty input and requests cancellation on a controlled second poll. Its suspended queue checks that four accepted attempts produce four terminal callbacks even after cooperative cancellation is requested.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The trace worksheet records one Work interval and its Projection child, actual thread attribution, and the relevant self/inclusive stack relationship. Until a capture exists, these observation cells remain blank. If selected samples identify membership descendants, the candidate substitutes Set membership while preserving ordered output. If decoding dominates, the projection hypothesis is weakened and the next experiment investigates decoding. No predicted saving becomes a measured result.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The confirmation sheet preserves attempt order, fixture, configuration, worker count, pressure and image state. It retains failures and cancellations beside successful latencies. Native exports begin as native-unannotated because device, OS build, revision and effective configuration still need evidence. A generic simulator build can succeed without a working runtime; record that limitation rather than marking simulator interaction complete. This worked answer supplies a concrete setup and interpretation contract. The learner must supply any saved trace, actual device samples, presentation checks and production review.\u003c/p>"
