        "story": "A bus inspector writes down every scheduled trip. For each one, the sheet records its number, route, departure and outcome. Two cancelled trips stay on the sheet even though they have no successful journey time. To compare buses, the inspector keeps the route and stopping rules the same. A practice sheet uses made-up times to check the calculator. Those numbers can prove the calculator works, but they cannot show whether any real bus was faster or deserves a new timetable.",
