      "exercise": {
        "brief": "Write three evidence requests: one for a symbol mismatch, one for possible jetsam, and one for a failed test job. Execute only checks with real supported inputs.",
        "steps": [
          "Run the checked-multiplication example and its overflow rejection cases.",
          "Use wrong-identity.json to identify the mismatching symbol metadata.",
          "For each of the three cases, name the original artifact needed to test its hypothesis.",
          "Inspect installed xcresulttool help; extract a summary only if a real scratch result bundle exists.",
          "Ask an independent reviewer to challenge one hypothesis, then revise the evidence and retest plan."
        ],
        "acceptance": [
          "The jetsam case contains no invented app backtrace.",
          "Each symbol match requires the reported image UUID and architecture.",
          "Synthetic text remains unable to satisfy captured diagnostic evidence.",
          "Cancelled and skipped test coverage stays visible.",
          "A reproduced mechanism and observed recovery after repair have separate evidence."
        ],
        "solution": "\u003cp>Case one has synthetic metadata with a mismatching dSYM UUID. Report the mismatch, not a crash cause. Request the original crash, distributed image identity and retained matching symbols; a rebuild of the same source is not a substitute. Case two describes disappearance under memory pressure but supplies no jetsam file. Request that report, identify the terminated process and use its own page size. Then plan an ownership recording. Host overflow checks establish safe arithmetic, while the memory hypothesis stays unresolved.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Case three concerns a test job. Retain the existing xcresult bundle if one exists, record scheme/configuration/destination and test filters, and extract its summary with the installed command. Without a bundle, mark extraction pending. A reviewer might change the hypothesis from product timeout to test-run cancellation; the revised case then asks for cancellation timing, completed/skipped tests, and whether the app remained responsive. Repeat the affected scratch row rather than accepting the old green console line.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Containment belongs to the release or feature owner and states its installed-client limits. Mechanism acceptance requires a controlled reproducer and before/after result for the repaired transition. Recovery acceptance requires comparable attempted operations and diagnostic coverage in a declared cohort/window. The result file, trace, symbolication, device reproduction, and observed recovery are intentionally absent here. The honest worked answer therefore closes local arithmetic and metadata checks, identifies the next collector, and leaves operational claims pending until actual artifacts are reviewed.\u003c/p>"
      },
