        "solution": "\u003cp>The counterexample begins with a rule that accepts any zero-blocker record. Add a required localization after review. The old rule still accepts evidence that never covered it. The corrected mechanism includes required resources in the fingerprint, checks attachment digests and matches evidence sourceRevision to the candidate. The Swift teaching gate also checks current reviewedRevision and testedRevision. Run the rejection cases on the changed inputs. This revision closes a concrete stale-acceptance gap; it does not merely ask reviewers to be more careful.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Run the provided stale-review, changed-bytes, architecture, blocker, and self-review cases and retain actual stdout from that execution. Attach a separate review note saying which counterexample the reviewer ran, why it failed the original rule, and how the changed behavior closes it. The supplied fixture's synthetic peer is not that review note. If no independent reviewer participates, leave independent critique pending and report only the automated checks actually obtained.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The conditional decision accepts local consistency reporting within the documented small-file scope. It leaves provenance authentication, UI cancellation, target membership, signed installation, device diagnostics, and observed consumer adoption to named future checks. If a later bundle workload changes the memory constraint, propose streaming hashing and rerun digest-equivalence and cancellation tests before acceptance. Retain the baseline tool and prior reports so a defective schema can be contained by rerunning affected records. This is concrete staff delivery evidence for one bounded feature, not a fabricated organizational outcome.\u003c/p>"
