        "scenario": "A made-up synchronous appointment function evaluates (try? service.appointments()) ?? [] and calls onSuccess. A later version stores onSuccess in a handler so it can call it after the function has returned.",
        "androidBridge": "Kotlin runCatching followed by getOrDefault(emptyList()) can erase failures like Swift try? followed by ?? []. Kotlin callbacks have no direct @escaping counterpart: Swift uses the annotation to permit a plain closure parameter to outlive its call, without specifying a thread or dispatcher.",
