        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>\u003ccode>try?\u003c/code> turns a thrown error into nil. The following \u003ccode>?? []\u003c/code> turns that nil into an empty list. Now an offline failure and a successful empty response both call onSuccess with no appointments. The caller cannot choose retry correctly. Keep separate success and failure paths with \u003ccode>do/catch\u003c/code>, or pass the error to the caller that owns the decision.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The original synchronous callbacks need no escaping annotation because they run before the consumer returns. Once the plain callback parameter is stored, mark that parameter \u003ccode>@escaping\u003c/code> and review the retaining handler and captured objects. Escaping permits a longer lifetime; it establishes neither background execution nor weak capture. Define how often completion can occur and when the handler releases the callback. Test nonempty success, empty success, and offline independently, including cleanup when delayed work is abandoned.\u003c/p>",
