        "scenario": "ReviewOwner stores a refresh callback using weak self and calls a protocol service that can throw. Save the callback elsewhere and invoke it. Then clear the outside owner variable and invoke the saved callback again.",
        "androidBridge": "Android sealed outcomes and an injected interface support the same separation of empty success from failure. Kotlin callback storage can retain an owner, but JVM garbage collection and Swift ARC have different cycle behavior; weak capture does not implement a LifecycleOwner-style stop policy.",
