        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>\u003ccode>makeUIViewController\u003c/code> creates the UIKit controller for this represented identity. \u003ccode>updateUIViewController\u003c/code> passes current SwiftUI inputs to that same controller. For example, changing a message from Ready to Saved should update its label rather than rebuild the controller. If the display method needs loaded views, deliberately load the hierarchy before assigning the text.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The representable's coordinator carries delegate and callback integration across temporary wrapper values. Update its current closure or binding when inputs change; retaining the initial wrapper forever can deliver edits to obsolete state. Compare existing and incoming text before assignment when unnecessary writes would disturb selection or focus, and avoid treating a state synchronization as a new user edit. Teardown can detach delegates and cancel subscriptions owned by this bridge, with an explicit lifetime policy. It must not cancel a shared operation merely because one wrapper disappears. The representable coordinator solves interoperability lifetime, while navigation ownership and hosted-controller containment remain separate decisions.\u003c/p>",
