        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>An RFC is a request for comments on a proposed decision. Describe the made-up large-list cost and the rule: keep the first complete value in input order with case-sensitive IDs. Name mapper, consumer, build, and rollout owners. Compare scans, a set with extra memory, and async mapping with new transfer and lifetime duties. Recommend conditionally: changed duplicate behavior or negligible user benefit can reject the candidate.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Sequence characterization fixtures, an old-path adapter, candidate equivalence, representative measurement, graph integration, controlled rollout, and removal. Require full-value comparisons and stable-ID selection checks, then accessibility, approved telemetry, and source/test inclusion in the relevant graphs. Pure shadow comparison is permitted by the absence of side effects. Define containment through the previous mapper only for installed clients that contain and honor that choice; it cannot downgrade binaries or undo unrelated data changes. Set removal criteria and an owner for migration debt. Mark device, archive, and production outcomes pending until artifacts exist instead of asking reviewers to approve an already-proven improvement.\u003c/p>",
