        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A resource enters the product through its target's declaration, not its folder name. Follow the file through processing, membership, generated support, owning bundle, and lookup. \u003ccode>Bundle.main\u003c/code> names the running process's main bundle, which differs for an app, test host, or extension. SwiftPM generates \u003ccode>Bundle.module\u003c/code> for the resource-owning target. That owner can expose a deliberate loader instead of assuming consumers know the bundle layout.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The process rule requests supported resource transformations; copy preserves specified content or structure. A static code product can still require a separate resource bundle. Asset catalogs, localized tables, and fonts have additional processing or registration contracts. The JSON loader should distinguish missing lookup from read failure, malformed decoding, and unsupported schema rather than returning a generic empty result. Test known, absent, and corrupt fixtures through the correct owner. Then inspect applicable consumer packaging and actual lookup. A host decoding test proves its package fixture, not an app archive, extension bundle, translated UI, font registration, or privacy-manifest sufficiency.\u003c/p>",
