        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Attach coordinates to green: source, graph route, dependency pins, toolchain, configuration, test plan, destination, environment, and fixture. Test-plan options choose execution behavior; Debug and Release are build configurations. Record expected, discovered, executed, skipped, and retried cases, plus filters. Otherwise a green result might mean the relevant tests never ran. A host pass supports only the host contract it exercised.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Build-for-testing compiles app and test products and prepares execution metadata; it does not run them. Test-without-building consumes those products. The pair needs compatible source, graph, conditions, resources, compiler, architecture, and SDK inputs. A relevant input change requires rebuilding rather than using arbitrary cached products. Retain separate build and execution outcomes, including first-failure and retry artifacts. A host resource test proves that package fixture's lookup and decoding, not app signing, extension packaging, minimum-runtime behavior, or a physical device. Likewise, a workflow declaration is configured evidence until actual run artifacts establish execution.\u003c/p>",
