        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A source file is the text you edit. An executable is the program the compiler makes from it. Running \u003ccode>swift First.swift\u003c/code> uses the driver to compile and execute that file. \u003ccode>swiftc First.swift -o First\u003c/code> produces an executable that is subsequently launched separately. Record the selected toolchain, command and output; neither route verifies the company iOS target or simulator integration.\u003c/p>\u003cp>String interpolation puts the current value into new text. It is like writing one on a card: changing the counter later does not rewrite the card. The caption therefore contains one, even though the later counter value is two. Printing the already constructed String does not reevaluate its earlier expression or create reactive state. Move construction after the update when the intended caption should describe the updated value. A successful toolchain version command alone proves tool selection, not behavior. If the file is missing, check its path. If Swift rejects a type, read the compiler diagnostic. These failures need different next steps.\u003c/p>",
