        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Let means this binding cannot be reassigned. Trying to give it another value is a compiler error, so that version never runs. Keep let for the unchanged synthetic name, or use var for that binding if reassignment is a real requirement. Converting every declaration to var removes useful constraints without explaining the bug.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The old caption is a separate problem. It is like a card saying attempt one after the counter has moved to two. It may compile correctly because it constructed a String before the attempt counter changed. Construct the caption after the intended update, then predict and compare the printed result. Do not claim var makes text reactive: it only permits reassignment. Keep the failing source or its error message alongside the working result. Record the source, command and expected/observed output so the correction is reviewable. These two checks establish local binding and evaluation rules, not app lifecycle, thread safety or deployment correctness.\u003c/p>",
