        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Choose the duplicate rule first: each occurrence adds one to that label’s count. Increment a Dictionary’s default Int subscript so general becomes two and dental/vision each become one. Print keys in sorted order when deterministic presentation is required; the order seen during dictionary traversal is not a display guarantee.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For the unique list, use a Set as a guest checklist and an Array as the arrival log. Append to the Array only when the Set says the label is new. That yields general, dental, vision in encounter order. Converting to Set and back would establish uniqueness while losing the requested ordering relationship. Hashing locates possible matches and equality decides membership; collisions are allowed, and hashValue is not a durable identifier. Test a changed input beginning with vision to show that encounter order changes while sorted histogram order remains separate. If equal labels represent different entities, use stable domain keys instead of display text.\u003c/p>",
