        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>A shimmer looking smooth alone tells you only about that isolated case. It does not identify why the full feed hitches. Define the failing workload: fixture list size, images, scroll path, window size, text size, destination, and warm/cold conditions. Capture representative frame hitches and relevant main-thread work rather than deriving performance from source or animation duration. App preparation and transaction submission can be delayed; render composition can also miss deadlines after a timely commit.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Check whether app-side layout, state updates or image preparation delay submission. Separately check rendering costs such as masks, effects and drawing overlapping content, called overdraw. A presentation-layer sample is useful for retargeting but is not a frame trace. CATransaction.flush is not a justified per-event fix and can alter batching without solving the cause.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Name who reproduces the workload and who owns the limited implementation experiment. Compare alternatives such as reducing preparation work or simplifying the expensive visual effect, preserve the baseline, and specify a rollback switch. Verify cancellation, latest-command model state, Reduced Motion, and accessible activation alongside timing. Report which traces were actually captured and which remain pending. The course's inspected shimmer and compiled lab are source/API evidence; neither supplies device measurements for this feed.\u003c/p>",
