        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>The old credential still appearing in memory does not make its refresh token valid. The server consumed that token during rotation, but the vault failed to save its replacement. In this mock, an unlocked retry is denied because there is no reconciliation endpoint or rotation grace rule. The checked recovery is explicit reauthentication. A real integration may use provider-documented reconciliation, but cannot infer replay safety from a transport or storage error.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Let the account service own one refresh operation shared by callers. Canceling one caller’s wait should not automatically cancel other waiters or log out the account. The compact fixture is single-caller and does not verify coalescing. Logout invalidates ownership and closes local authorization even if credential deletion fails.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Save a properly protected sign-out or cleanup obligation. On restart, check it before restoring any credential that survived in the vault. Classify interaction restrictions separately from item absence and configuration errors. Verification should include late refresh completion, post-rotation storage failure, denied retry and recovery. Fake-vault checks establish state decisions; signed Keychain availability, durable sign-out and real provider rotation semantics remain separate work.\u003c/p>",
