        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Ask whether the process ended or stayed alive but unresponsive. Record the operation state, exact build, device, OS and time. A raw crash report supports exception or termination analysis and thread stacks. A hang needs sampled stacks or a timeline covering the unresponsive interval. Jetsam is a memory-pressure termination. Its report describes memory pressure and process selection; it does not provide app thread backtraces.\u003c/p>\u003cp>For CI, collect the actual xcresult test-result bundle. Keep its invocation, destination, selected tests, retries and cancellation or skip status with it. That bundle cannot substitute for a field crash diagnostic. Before trusting application symbol names, I compare image UUID and architecture with retained executable and dSYM evidence.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Without the files, these are requests for evidence and possible explanations. They are not a diagnosis. I name each collector, preserve original bytes, and select a reproducer that could separate mechanisms. A red job and an unresponsive screen may be unrelated. Command help or a synthetic fixture proves neither runtime diagnosis nor operational recovery.\u003c/p>",
