        "answerHTML": "\u003cp>Zero blockers may describe an old review. A new requirement changes what must be accepted, like a checklist gaining another required item. The revised gate must bind required resources, artifact identity, evidence paths and content digests to the reviewed fingerprint. A digest summarizes bytes; the fingerprint identifies the decision inputs that were reviewed. Evidence must name the current source revision, and retest must exercise the affected new requirement.\u003c/p>\u003cp>The Swift model requires currentRevision, reviewedRevision and testedRevision to match. It rejects an empty reviewer or the author as reviewer, and throws if blockers remain. Sendable on immutable review values permits safe transfer; it neither schedules work nor authenticates the reviewer. The Python companion adds actual path and digest consistency checks.\u003c/p>\u003cp>Test cases that must fail: a changed requirement, old review, changed attachment bytes, self-review and a blocker accepted merely to meet a deadline. The independent reviewer inspects the revised artifact and closure evidence. If no person participated, automated structural checks can pass while actual independent critique remains pending. Fixture labels cannot fill that gap.\u003c/p>",
